{"name":"Citadel Blue","hex":"#9eabad","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"citadel","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A strong fortress that sits high above a city.","A stronghold or fortified place."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/citadel"},{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"}],"entries":[{"title":"Citadel","blocks":[{"text":"A citadel is the most fortified area of a town or city. It may be a castle, fortress, or fortified center. The term is a diminutive of city, meaning \"little city\", because it is a smaller part of the city of which it is the defensive core."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/Casale_Monferrato_map_%28018_003%29.jpg/330px-Casale_Monferrato_map_%28018_003%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Citadel"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Bibracte_Porte_Rebout.jpg/500px-Bibracte_Porte_Rebout.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Bibracte_Porte_Rebout.jpg/500px-Bibracte_Porte_Rebout.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Reconstruction of the redoubt of Bibracte, a part of the Gaulish oppidum. The Celts utilized these fortified cities in the 2nd and 1st centuries BC.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABibracte_Porte_Rebout.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Si%C3%A9ge_de_la_flotte_turc.jpg/500px-Si%C3%A9ge_de_la_flotte_turc.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Si%C3%A9ge_de_la_flotte_turc.jpg/1280px-Si%C3%A9ge_de_la_flotte_turc.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Si%C3%A9ge_de_la_flotte_turc.jpg/500px-Si%C3%A9ge_de_la_flotte_turc.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Although much of Nice was ransacked during the 1543 siege of the city, Franco-Ottoman forces besieging Nice were unable to capture its Citadel. Citadels have often been used as a last defence for a besieged army.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASi%C3%A9ge_de_la_flotte_turc.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Royal_22e_R%C3%A9giment_-_panoramio.jpg/500px-Royal_22e_R%C3%A9giment_-_panoramio.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, htt